Hyphenator: do not load the missing "am" pattern file

Upstream: platform/frameworks/base commit 67ed6fce130422fa70c33b8822b30c7644fc10ef
  "Remove call to `addHyphenator("am", 1, 1)`"
  Author Michael Hoisie, 2025-08-05; committed 2025-08-06.
  Change-Id I8ae35baff1d2c4996a48d8b614361b20c252a108, Bug 436377626.
  First tagged in android-16.0.0_r4 (not in r1, r2 or r3).
Diff fetched unchanged from
  https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/base/+/67ed6fce130422fa70c33b8822b30c7644fc10ef%5E%21/

Why: the official library (BLR2.250402.052) has it. In its Hyphenator
init() the short-string constants passed to addHyphenator go "af"
(movw $0x6661), "as" ($0x7361), "be" ($0x6562) with no "am" ($0x6d61) in
between; the only "am" left is the later addHyphenatorAlias("am",
"und-Ethi"). Our r1 build has "am" in both places. hyph-am.hyb does not
exist, so r1 only logs "Unable to find pattern file or unable to map it
for am" at every Hyphenator init; with the change that error is gone and
Amharic still resolves through the und-Ethi alias.

diff --git a/core/jni/android_text_Hyphenator.cpp b/core/jni/android_text_Hyphenator.cpp
index e45cbaf..d9abe26 100644
--- a/core/jni/android_text_Hyphenator.cpp
+++ b/core/jni/android_text_Hyphenator.cpp
@@ -127,8 +127,7 @@
     constexpr int INDIC_MIN_PREFIX = 2;
     constexpr int INDIC_MIN_SUFFIX = 2;
 
-    addHyphenator("af", 1, 1);  // Afrikaans
-    addHyphenator("am", 1, 1);  // Amharic
+    addHyphenator("af", 1, 1);                                // Afrikaans
     addHyphenator("as", INDIC_MIN_PREFIX, INDIC_MIN_SUFFIX);  // Assamese
     addHyphenator("be", 2, 2);  // Belarusian
     addHyphenator("bg", 2, 2);  // Bulgarian
